{"id":"d06406f9c94b474960cdda5f3e6e8f1b0353a854","axis":"silent","repo":"elastic/elasticsearch","sha":"d06406f9c94b474960cdda5f3e6e8f1b0353a854","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/changelog/167492.yaml","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+area: ES|QL","+issues: []","+pr: 167492","+summary: Report the DESCRIBE columns in column metadata","+type: enhancement"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/reference/query-languages/esql/_snippets/generated/x-pack-esql/commands/settings/column_metadata.md","lines":["@@ -5,7 +5,9 @@"," serverless: preview"," stack: preview 9.5.0"," ```","-When enabled, column metadata is added to the `_query` response as additional `_meta` properties. Defaults to `false`. Currently, only `_meta.bucket` is added for columns corresponding to the `BUCKET` function and contains bucket interval and unit for queries where it can be determined.","+When enabled, column metadata is added to the `_query` response as additional `_meta` properties. Defaults to `false`. `_meta.bucket` is added for columns corresponding to the `BUCKET` function and contains bucket interval and unit for queries where it can be determined.","+","+{applies_to}`{\"stack\": \"preview 9.7+\", \"serverless\": \"preview\"}` Every column also reports what `DESCRIBE` reports about it, other than its name and type, under the same names: `role`, `field`, `origin`, `metric_type`, `unit`, `interval`, `time_zone` and `description`. Values that are not known are left out, and a value with several entries is a list."," "," {applies_to}`{\"stack\": \"ga 9.6+\", \"serverless\": \"unavailable\"}` The default itself is configurable. If a query does not specify a value, the `esql.query.settings.column_metadata` cluster setting supplies it. If that cluster setting is not configured either, the value is `false`."," "],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/reference/query-languages/esql/kibana/generated/x-pack-esql/definition/settings/column_metadata.json","lines":["@@ -7,5 +7,5 @@","   \"serverlessOnly\" : false,","   \"preview\" : true,","   \"snapshotOnly\" : false,","-  \"description\" : \"When enabled, column metadata is added to the `_query` response as additional `_meta` properties. Defaults to `false`. Currently, only `_meta.bucket` is added for columns corresponding to the `BUCKET` function and contains bucket interval and unit for queries where it can be determined.\\n\\n{applies_to}`{\\\"stack\\\": \\\"ga 9.6+\\\", \\\"serverless\\\": \\\"unavailable\\\"}` The default itself is configurable. If a query does not specify a value, the `esql.query.settings.column_metadata` cluster setting supplies it. If that cluster setting is not configured either, the value is `false`.\"","+  \"description\" : \"When enabled, column metadata is added to the `_query` response as additional `_meta` properties. Defaults to `false`. `_meta.bucket` is added for columns corresponding to the `BUCKET` function and contains bucket interval and unit for queries where it can be determined.\\n\\n{applies_to}`{\\\"stack\\\": \\\"preview 9.7+\\\", \\\"serverless\\\": \\\"preview\\\"}` Every column also reports what `DESCRIBE` reports about it, other than its name and type, under the same names: `role`, `field`, `origin`, `metric_type`, `unit`, `interval`, `time_zone` and `description`. Values that are not known are left out, and a value with several entries is a list.\\n\\n{applies_to}`{\\\"stack\\\": \\\"ga 9.6+\\\", \\\"serverless\\\": \\\"unavailable\\\"}` The default itself is configurable. If a query does not specify a value, the `esql.query.settings.column_metadata` cluster setting supplies it. If that cluster setting is not configured either, the value is `false`.\""," }"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/grouping/BucketColumnMetadataIT.java","lines":["@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@ public void testBucketColumnMetadata() {","        